From d1ff780f2c07cdca570d633de4aa574cb01d175b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jorge Marques <jorge.marques@analog.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2025 21:20:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 117/190] i3c: master: Add inline i3c_readl_fifo() and
 i3c_writel_fifo()

commit 73251577bb90ef3172dbfbfe67e8470a3f692eb8 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

The I3C abstraction expects u8 buffers, but some controllers operate with
a 32-bit bus width FIFO and cannot flag valid bytes individually. To avoid
reading or writing outside the buffer bounds, use 32-bit accesses where
possible and apply memcpy for any remaining bytes

Signed-off-by: Jorge Marques <jorge.marques@analog.com>
Suggested-by: Wolfram Sang <wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com>
Reviewed-by: Wolfram Sang <wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com>
Tested-by: Wolfram Sang <wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com>
Reviewed-by: Frank Li <Frank.Li@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexandre Belloni <alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20250624-i3c-writesl-readsl-v3-1-63ccf0870f01@analog.com
State: upstream (733b439375b494e8a6950ab47d18a4b615b73cb3)
Message-ID: <20250925155006.3080413-4-manikanta.guntupalli@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
